@startuml ddc_acquisition_activity
!include dark-theme.puml
title DDC acquisition lifecycle - full refresh and targeted recovery

start

:Acquisition trigger;
if (Targeted recovery request?) then (yes)
  :Snapshot only the failed/read-degraded row\non the dispatcher;
  if (Already healthy, explicitly powered off this runtime,\nor write busy?) then (yes)
    :Skip this candidate pass;
    stop
  else (probe)
    :Enumerate current displays off dispatcher;
    :Match requested ID, retained instance path / DeviceID,\nEDID key / serial, port form, then adapter name;
    if (Matching display found?) then (no)
      :Keep Failed and retry on a later worker pass;
      stop
    else (yes)
    endif
  endif
else (full Refresh)
  :Latest-request-wins scheduler enumerates off dispatcher;
  note right
    Constructor bootstrap is the one synchronous enumeration.
    Public topology/settings refreshes never run CCD, registry,
    or WMI enumeration on their caller thread.
  end note
  :Post fresh snapshot reconcile to dispatcher;
  :Reconcile identity and park missing known-DDC rows as Failed;
  if (Recent topology event?) then (yes)
    :Wait remaining post-detection settle window;
  else (no)
  endif
  :Phase B probes enumerated displays sequentially;
endif

:Read resolved brightness VCP with retry;
note right $TINT_GREEN
  Every failed native GET retires only that monitor's helper.
  The next retry launches a fresh process, performs lightweight
  Win32 + EDID identity resolution, and opens new physical handles.
  Final acquisition attempt also refreshes the parent snapshot while
  preserving a user brightness-VCP override.
end note

if (Read succeeds?) then (yes)
  if (Existing MonitorInfo?) then (yes)
    :Install fresh DDC entry / maximum / projections;
    if (Has explicit user/profile slider value?) then (yes)
      :Preserve manual slider baseline;
    else (no)
      :Sync slider baseline from current DDC read\nwithout claiming user intent;
    endif
    :Recover curve-aware SliderState;
  else (no)
    :Create MonitorInfo from current DDC read;
    :Saved profile may later restore manual UI state;
  endif
  :Clear read-degraded/error state and retained recovery identity;
  :Mark row acquired;
else (no)
  if (Targeted recovery and eligible manual row has\na previously verified projected bus value?) then (yes)
    :Send one minimally-invasive write transport probe;
    if (SET transport accepted?) then (yes)
      :Attempt one immediate GET;
      if (Reply recovered?) then (yes)
        :Promote fully from the returned brightness;
        :Mark row acquired;
      else (no)
        :Publish explicit ReadDegraded compatibility state;
        :Keep LastDDCError and recovery candidacy;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Reset this monitor's helper transport;
      :Keep Failed and retained recovery identity;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Add or keep row as Failed;
    :Retain immutable recovery identity;
    :Raise DDCRecoveryRequested for known-capable rows;
    :No arbitrary acquisition write;
  endif
endif

:Apply per-row bounds, norm curve, and dwell projections;
:Record sticky DDC-capable observation;

if (Full refresh?) then (yes)
  :Consume explicit topology/VCP replay generation;
  if (Hardware state was invalidated?) then (yes)
    :Invalidate pending + verified target state;
    :Queue explicit manual replay only after fresh handles/maxima;
  else (no)
  endif
endif

:Raise MonitorsRefreshed;

if (Brightness curve enabled?) then (yes)
  :EnvironmentalCurveService evaluates immediately\nand queues current curve-owned targets;
else (no)
  :No additional write;
endif

:Recompute master slider from connected\nhardware-functional displays using MasterSliderMode;

if (Fully readable row was marked acquired?) then (yes)
  :Clear stale runtime power-off suppression;
  :Resolve final post-subscriber SliderState owner;
  if (Current manual or curve owner target exists?) then (yes)
    :ReplayRecoveredBrightnessIntent;
    :Force through zero-cooldown scheduler;
    :SET + normal matching read-back verification;
  else (Disabled / no intent)
    :No recovery brightness write;
  endif
else (no)
endif

note right
  Master recompute is UI-only. MonitorsRefreshed subscribers finish
  synchronous curve and master reconciliation before MonitorService
  resolves the recovered row's final hardware owner.

  A successful acquisition GET proves that replies resumed, not that
  firmware visibly applied the value it reports. The forced replay is
  one recovery-boundary SET, not a periodic reapply loop, and it still
  requires matching read-back before persistence or dedupe.
end note

stop
@enduml
